### [6] Login — Admin (captura token automaticamente)
POST {{base_url}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@teste.com",
  "senha": "admin123"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("token_admin", response.body.token);
  client.test("Login admin OK", function() { client.assert(response.status === 200); });
%}

###

### [7] Logout (invalida sessão no servidor)
POST {{base_url}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token_candidato}}

> {%
  client.test("Logout OK", function() {
    client.assert(response.status === 200 || response.status === 204);
  });
%}

###

### ── TESTES DE ERRO ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### [8] Login com senha incorreta (deve retornar 401)
POST {{base_url}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "joao.candidato@teste.com",
  "senha": "senha_errada"
}

> {%
  client.test("Senha errada bloqueada", function() {
    client.assert(response.status === 401);
  });
%}

###

### [9] Login com e-mail inexistente (deve retornar 401)
POST {{base_url}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nao.existe@teste.com",
  "senha": "qualquer"
}

> {%
  client.test("Email inexistente bloqueado", function() {
    client.assert(response.status === 401);
  });
%}

###

### [10] Registro com e-mail inválido (deve retornar 400)
POST {{base_url}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nome": "Teste",
  "email": "email-invalido",
  "senha": "senha123",
  "dataNascimento": "1990-01-01T00:00:00",
  "tipoUsuario": "CANDIDATO"
}

> {%
  client.test("Email inválido rejeitado", function() {
    client.assert(response.status === 400);
  });
%}

###

### [11] Re-login do candidato para restaurar token após logout
POST {{base_url}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "joao.candidato@teste.com",
  "senha": "senha123"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("token_candidato", response.body.token);
  client.test("Re-login candidato OK", function() { client.assert(response.status === 200); });
%}

###
